    "summary": "Soaring Comes A Time & Keith's debut shine in high‑energy set",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a soaring version of Comes A Time with Jerry’s falsetto on fire, while Keith Godchaux makes an impressive keyboard debut throughout the Other One/Cryptical suite. Jack Straw, Tennessee Jed and Mexicali Blues are tight and energetic, making this one of the stronger 1971 performances.",
    "review": "The October 19, 1971 night at Northrop Auditorium captures the Dead at a pivotal moment – Keith Godchaux’s first show with the band adds fresh color to an already high‑energy set. The band launches into a blistering Comes A Time where Jerry’s soaring falsetto and bright guitar cut through a crystal‑clear mix, then rolls straight into a tight run of classics like Jack Straw, Tennessee Jed and Mexicali Blues. In the second set the Cryptical Envelopment → Drums → The Other One → Cryptical sequence unfolds with Keith’s left‑hand/right‑hand piano split sounding almost three‑dimensional, while Bill keeps an unshakable pocket throughout. Wharf Rat closes the night on a soulful note, rounding out a performance that feels both tight and exploratory, all captured in an excellent soundboard tape that lets every nuance shine.",
